From: Benjamin Ang <hello@benjaminang.tv>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:28:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix: 1.4.1 candidate follow-up - CLI flags in queries,
 grep host-marker overhead, captured-section bounds

Written by Grok Bot (box), reviewed against the plugin's per-result harness and
30-turn replay; not by the local model.

- format_adapters._query_selectors: skip command-line options (-n, --stat).
  The plugin's query carries the tool command; '-n' was a 'strong' selector
  that displaced the searched name, so an all-matching rg -n result had no hit,
  the saturated mode never ran and the plugin's brief lost the definition.
- agent_formats grep render: with a caller gap_marker, fully omitted files keep
  their header and share one marker per consecutive run (25-file rg: ~2.5 KB of
  host markers -> one). Default '[... N matches omitted ...]' unchanged.
- agent_formats: InliningGapMarker honoured in the grep adapter and the
  test-runner renderer (inline_short_gaps).
- pytest captured sections: end at the next rule/test header/section header
  (captured stdout may contain blank lines); keep first and last line instead
  of first 2 / last 2 (WARNING+ and error-fingerprint lines still kept, query
  hits still restored).
- tests: test_grep_cross_file_marker_141.py, test_pytest_captured_sections.py
  (updated + 3 new); all new ones fail without the fix.

Default path unchanged: run_battery 15/15 with identical savings,
threshold_sweep identical. Engine suite 1159 passed, 3 skipped (was 1151).
